                <pb facs="0587" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/2629: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Then in France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-17">August 17, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your 66, August 17, 9 a.m. While the American Government deplores the terrible
                    strife in Spain and devoutly wishes for peace at the earliest possible moment,
                    our policy, as already announced, is to “scrupulously refrain from any
                    interference whatever in the unfortunate Spanish situation”. (See telegraphic
                    circular of August 7 last.)</p>
                <p>In these circumstances, you should not attend this proposed meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
